#Problem APEX 2.5.9

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Differentiation)
## DBsection(Chain rule (with trigonometric functions))
## KEYWORDS('derivative', 'chain rule')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(2)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('2.5')
## Problem1('9')
## Edited July 2023

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric")->variables->are(t => "Real");

$a = random(2, 9) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$b = random(2, 9) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$c = random(3, 6);
$k = random(2, 6);

$c1 = $c - 1;
$kc = $k * $c;

$ans = Formula("$kc($a sin(t) + $b cos(t))^{$c1}($a cos(t) - $b sin(t))");

BEGIN_PGML
Compute the derivative of the given function.

[```
  g(t) = [$k] ([$a] \sin t + [$b] \cos t)^{[$c]}
```]

    [` g'(t) = `][_]{$ans}{25}.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Use the Chain Rule with inside function [`u = [$a] \sin t + [$b] \cos t`]
and outside function [`y = [$k] u^{[$c]}`].

[``
  \begin{aligned}
    g'(t) &= \frac{dy}{du} \cdot \frac{du}{dt}\\
    &= [$kc] u^{[$c1]} ([$a] \cos t - [$b] \sin t) \\
    &= [$kc] ([$a] \sin t + [$b] \cos t)^{[$c1]} ([$a] \cos t - [$b] \sin t) \\
  \end{aligned}
``]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    

